        {
          "candidate_id": "impact_claim_inconsistent_behavior_break_9aac4324_c0ee3376::canonical",
          "text": "The cancelTimestamp should be updated in all amendment scenarios, including when only amountInBase is amended, so an amendment with a new future cancelTimestamp revives the expired order.",
          "expression": {
            "op": "implies",
            "args": [
              {
                "var": "c9a3276f2_amendment_only_amount_changed"
              },
              {
                "op": "eq",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "var": "c9a3276f2_order_cancel_timestamp_after_amend"
                  },
                  {
                    "var": "c9a3276f2_amendment_new_cancel_timestamp"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "derivation": "canonical_formalization",
          "source_ids": [
            "intent_cancel_timestamp_updated_all_amendments"
          ],
          "evidence_ids": [
            "According to the project team, it is intended behavior that an expired order can be \"revived\" by amending it with a new, future `cancelTimestamp`. This functionality works as expected when the order's `price` or `side` is changed, as this flow is handled by `_executeAmendNewOrder`, which re-creates the order with all new parameters, including the new `cancelTimestamp`.",
            "To ensure consistent behavior and align with the protocol's intent, the `cancelTimestamp` should be updated in all amendment scenarios.",
            "In the `_processAmend` function, before branching into `_executeAmendNewOrder` or `_executeAmendAmount`, unconditionally update the `order.cancelTimestamp`.",
            "Alternatively, add `order.cancelTimestamp = uint32(args.cancelTimestamp);` inside the `_executeAmendAmount` function."
          ],
          "checkpoints": {
            "raw": {
              "c9a3276f2_amendment_new_cancel_timestamp": "amendment input",
              "c9a3276f2_amendment_only_amount_changed": "amendment input",
              "c9a3276f2_order_cancel_timestamp_after_amend": "after amendment processing"
            },
            "normalized": {
              "c9a3276f2_amendment_new_cancel_timestamp": "before",
              "c9a3276f2_amendment_only_amount_changed": "before",
              "c9a3276f2_order_cancel_timestamp_after_amend": "after"
            }
          },
